        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "myjSA",
          "x": 1229,
          "y": 39,
          "name": "Temperature adjustment — 320°C",
          "context": "Temperature target adjustment, not live measured temperature. Firmware evidence: source/Core/Threads/UI/logic/TemperatureAdjust.cpp and source/Core/Threads/UI/drawing/color_160x80/draw_temperature_change.cpp. Initial held buttons are ignored until release. F short increments and B short decrements by configured short step; holds use configured long step and accelerate. ReverseButtonTempChangeEnabled swaps direction, so plus/minus display marks reverse with the button setting. Default draw has PLUS LEFT and MINUS RIGHT. OK short or long, or both buttons, saves and exits to previous screen; three seconds idle also saves/exits. No Cancel action. Units C/F; three digits support temperatures through 850F. Typography: Space Grotesk only, using existing size tokens (15px settings labels, 19px settings values, and 30px temperature digits where needed), weight 600. Reuse raster glyph sets; do not introduce utility-only 12px or 24px font sizes. Verified at native 160x80 canvas size; hardware legibility remains to be checked on-device.",
          "reusable": true,
          "clip": true,
          "width": 160,
          "height": 80,
          "fill": "$section-solder-background",
          "layout": "none",
          "children": [
            {
